---
// How much data a live uses: bitrate × time, split across the SIMs. Same rule of thumb as the
// guide (docs/guide/concepts/data-plans.md): one hour at 2.5 Mbit/s is about 1.1 GB.
---

<div class="budget" data-budget>
	<label><span class="k">Stream <em data-out="rate"></em></span><input type="range" min="1" max="12" step="0.5" value="2.5" data-in="rate" /></label>
	<label><span class="k">Live per day <em data-out="hours"></em></span><input type="range" min="0.5" max="10" step="0.5" value="3" data-in="hours" /></label>
	<label><span class="k">Days <em data-out="days"></em></span><input type="range" min="1" max="60" step="1" value="30" data-in="days" /></label>
	<label><span class="k">SIMs <em data-out="sims"></em></span><input type="range" min="1" max="4" step="1" value="3" data-in="sims" /></label>
	<div class="figs">
		<div><span class="k">In all</span><strong data-out="total"></strong></div>
		<div><span class="k">Per SIM, even split</span><strong data-out="per"></strong></div>
		<div><span class="k">Per hour</span><strong data-out="hour"></strong></div>
	</div>
</div>

<script>
	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-budget]")) {
		const input = (k: string) => Number(root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`[data-in="${k}"]`)!.value);
		const out = (k: string, v: string) => {
			root.querySelector(`[data-out="${k}"]`)!.textContent = v;
		};
		const gb = (v: number) => (v >= 100 ? `${Math.round(v)} GB` : `${v.toFixed(1)} GB`);
		const update = () => {
			const [rate, hours, days, sims] = ["rate", "hours", "days", "sims"].map(input);
			const hour = (rate * 3600) / 8 / 1000;
			const total = hour * hours * days;
			out("rate", `${rate} Mbit/s`);
			out("hours", `${hours} h`);
			out("days", `${days}`);
			out("sims", `${sims}`);
			out("hour", gb(hour));
			out("total", gb(total));
			out("per", gb(total / sims));
		};
		root.addEventListener("input", update);
		update();
	}
</script>
